23-## 1. When to Use
24-
25:Use this skill when one or more apply:
26-- the task is mainly about delegation structure or collaboration topology
27-- A2A coordination, handoff quality, or inter-agent lifecycle control matters
28-- agent discovery or agent-card review is part of the decision
29-- long-running asynchronous coordination needs explicit state tracking
30-- coordinator logic, join contracts, or partial-state honesty materially affect correctness
31-- orchestration overhead, trust boundary, or capability-fit trade-offs can change the result
32-
33:Do not use this skill when:
34-- one coherent agent path is sufficient
35-- the task is mainly domain analysis, coding, or grounded research with only incidental delegation
36-- coordination vocabulary would mostly decorate a simpler workflow
37-
38-## 2. Primary Mission
